  "body": "### Keepalive: OFF\n<!-- meta:issue:660 -->\n\n### Source Issue #660: Route-weights export published source_version 0 (empty Brain) and overwrote an evidenced publication; bind the DB path and refuse evidence regressions\n\nBase: main\nHead: codex/issue-660\n\nSource: https://github.com/stranske/Orchestrator/issues/660\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nThe route-weights export published to `exports/route-weights/config/route-weights.json` at 2026-10-17T03:53:44Z carries `source_version: 0` and `evidence_ok: false` with `ranking: []` for every task type, while the live Brain at `~/.codex/orchestrator/feedback/orchestrator.db` is at weight version 68 with `implement` observations codex 1198, cursor 445, gemini 101, vibe 137, claude 450 (read-only check, 2026-10-17 04:30Z). Rebuilding the export from the live DB yields `implement` ranking length 4. The publisher therefore ran against an empty or wrong database and replaced an evidenced publication with an evidence-less one; the change detector accepted it because the content differed. Every consumer of the export (stranske/Workflows `agent_delegation_policy.js`, the intake chooser from Workflows#3991) now falls back to its static default, so the learned routing that Priority 3 depends on is silently off. Nothing reported it: `route_weights_export.py` neither binds the DB path explicitly nor refuses to publish a regression from evidenced to evidence-less content.\n\nCampaign concept (value-chain gate): situation = every daily export publish; demand = one publish per day plus every capacity-state change; pass number = the published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2 on every check, and the exporter's log shows one refused publish when fed an empty DB in the test; printed by `gh api repos/stranske/Orchestrator/contents/config/route-weights.json?ref=exports/route-weights` and the exporter's test. Check date: next daily export after merge, then the weekly check 2026-10-20.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [stranske/Orchestrator#575](https://github.com/stranske/Orchestrator/issues/575)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] Update `src/route_weights_export.py` to use the shared `feedback.py` DB resolver and log `db=<path> source_version=<n>` at the start of every run.\n- [x] Add `publish_guard(new_doc, published_doc) -> (ok, reason)` in `src/route_weights_export.py`; refuse publication and exit non-zero with the reason for the three regression conditions.\n- [x] Add `--allow-evidence-regression` to `src/route_weights_export.py` and log deliberate allowed regressions.\n- [x] Add tests in `tests/test_route_weights_export.py` for empty DB refusal, all-false evidence refusal, published-true/new-false refusal, flag allowance, and `ORCH_STATE_DIR` path resolution.\n- [x] Update the export README and `ARCHITECTURE.md` export paragraph with the guard.\n- [x] Update `orchestrate.sh` cadence logging to surface export-publish refusals.\n- [ ] Run one publish from the live DB after merge and mirror sync; record `source_version` and `implement` ranking length in the PR.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/test_route_weights_export.py` passes.\n- [ ] Making `publish_guard` return `(True, \"\")` unconditionally causes the empty-DB test to fail naming the guard; reverting it makes the test pass, with both outcomes captured in the PR body.\n- [ ] `python3 src/verify.py` passes.\n- [ ] The next published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Full Issue Text</summary>\n\n\n\n## Why\n\nThe route-weights export published to `exports/route-weights/config/route-weights.json` at 2026-10-17T03:53:44Z carries `source_version: 0` and `evidence_ok: false` with `ranking: []` for every task type, while the live Brain at `~/.codex/orchestrator/feedback/orchestrator.db` is at weight version 68 with `implement` observations codex 1198, cursor 445, gemini 101, vibe 137, claude 450 (read-only check, 2026-10-17 04:30Z). Rebuilding the export from the live DB yields `implement` ranking length 4. The publisher therefore ran against an empty or wrong database and replaced an evidenced publication with an evidence-less one; the change detector accepted it because the content differed. Every consumer of the export (stranske/Workflows `agent_delegation_policy.js`, the intake chooser from Workflows#3991) now falls back to its static default, so the learned routing that Priority 3 depends on is silently off. Nothing reported it: `route_weights_export.py` neither binds the DB path explicitly nor refuses to publish a regression from evidenced to evidence-less content.\n\nCampaign concept (value-chain gate): situation = every daily export publish; demand = one publish per day plus every capacity-state change; pass number = the published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2 on every check, and the exporter's log shows one refused publish when fed an empty DB in the test; printed by `gh api repos/stranske/Orchestrator/contents/config/route-weights.json?ref=exports/route-weights` and the exporter's test. Check date: next daily export after merge, then the weekly check 2026-10-20.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/route_weights_export.py`: resolve the feedback DB path explicitly (the same resolver `feedback.py` uses, with `ORCH_STATE_DIR` honoured) and log the resolved path and `source_version` on every run\n- a publish guard: refuse to publish when `source_version == 0`, when every task type has `evidence_ok: false`, or when the new document would set `evidence_ok` false for a task type the currently published document has true, unless `--allow-evidence-regression` is passed; print the refusal reason\n- tests for the path binding and the three refusal conditions\n- `orchestrate.sh` cadence step: surface the refusal in the tick log\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Do not change thresholds (`n_obs >= 20`), the 120-day window or the exclusion classes\n- Do not change the v1 schema or the capacity block\n- A guard that only logs and still publishes is not completion\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] In `src/route_weights_export.py`, replace the implicit DB lookup with the shared resolver from `feedback.py` and log `db=<path> source_version=<n>` at the start of every run.\n- [ ] Add `publish_guard(new_doc, published_doc) -> (ok, reason)` implementing the three refusal conditions; call it before any publish; exit non-zero with the reason when refused.\n- [ ] Add `--allow-evidence-regression` for a deliberate owner-approved downgrade, logged.\n- [ ] Add tests in `tests/test_route_weights_export.py`: empty DB \u2192 refused; all-false evidence \u2192 refused; published true \u2192 new false \u2192 refused; flag \u2192 allowed; path resolver honours `ORCH_STATE_DIR`.\n- [ ] Update the export README and the ARCHITECTURE.md export paragraph with the guard.\n- [ ] After merge and mirror sync, run one publish from the live DB and record `source_version` and `implement` ranking length in the PR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/test_route_weights_export.py` passes.\n- [ ] Deliberate-break gate: temporarily make `publish_guard` return `(True, \"\")` unconditionally; the empty-DB test fails naming the guard; revert and rerun green. Capture both outcomes in the PR body.\n- [ ] `python3 src/verify.py` passes.\n- [ ] The next published export has `source_version > 0` and `task_types.implement.ranking` length \u2265 2.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `src/route_weights_export.py:57-96, 226-234` (version read, retention rule, evidence flag)\n- `src/feedback.py:271-294` (window and eligibility), DB resolver\n- Orchestrator CLAUDE.md \u00a72 \"Learning-loop integrity\": a publication that drops evidence is a Brain-integrity event and belongs in that section's rules\n- Capability Program tracker stranske/Orchestrator#575, routing unit\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n\u2014\nPR created automatically to engage Codex.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:660 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #660\n\nCloses #660\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->",
